# Onboard radios only (openmanet_setup.sh ... -x onboardradioonly)
#
# boards/common/openmanet_diffconfig has a "# WIFI" block that force-enables a
# pile of EXTERNAL wifi cards as =y (iwlwifi ax200/ax210, ath9k, ath10k qca6174,
# ath11k wcn6855 + pci, mt76/mt7915/mt7916, owl-loader). That is right for the
# EKH boards, and it is inherited unconditionally by every board because it
# lives in boards/common.
#
# The Pi 3A+ civil SKU (#195) has NO PCIe and exactly ONE USB-A port, which the
# CM108 PTT adapter occupies in the shipping configuration. None of these cards
# can physically be attached. Measured cost if left in: ~25 MB installed.
#
# KEPT ON PURPOSE (do not add to this list):
#   kmod-brcmfmac + 43455 nvram/firmware  - the Pi onboard wifi. It must stay =y
#     and occupy radio0 so morse (HaLow) stays radio1; it is also the onboarding
#     AP, which on an eth-less 3A+ is the only field entry point. See -x mm6108only.
#   kmod-mac80211 / MAC80211_MESH / wpad-openssl / kmod-batman-adv - core mesh.
#
# CONFIG_PACKAGE_kmod-iwlwifi is not set
# CONFIG_PACKAGE_iwlwifi-firmware-ax200 is not set
# CONFIG_PACKAGE_iwlwifi-firmware-ax210 is not set
# CONFIG_PACKAGE_kmod-owl-loader is not set
# CONFIG_PACKAGE_kmod-ath11k is not set
# CONFIG_PACKAGE_kmod-ath11k-pci is not set
# CONFIG_PACKAGE_ath11k-firmware-wcn6855 is not set
# CONFIG_PACKAGE_kmod-ath10k is not set
# CONFIG_PACKAGE_ath10k-firmware-qca6174 is not set
# CONFIG_PACKAGE_kmod-ath9k is not set
# CONFIG_PACKAGE_kmod-ath9k-htc is not set
# CONFIG_PACKAGE_kmod-mt76 is not set
# CONFIG_PACKAGE_kmod-mt7915e is not set
# CONFIG_PACKAGE_kmod-mt7915-firmware is not set
# CONFIG_PACKAGE_kmod-mt7916-firmware is not set
#
# USB WiFi dongles too (decision 2026-09-30). #217 argues to KEEP these because a
# USB dongle is pluggable on a Pi - true for the Pi 4, but the civil 3A+ has ONE
# USB-A port and the shipping configuration commits it to the CM108 PTT adapter
# (#195), so a USB WiFi dongle physically cannot coexist. Dropped deliberately;
# this fragment is opt-in per board, so the Pi 4 line is free to keep them.
# NB kmod-ath9k-htc is the USB member of the ath9k family (HTC = its USB
# interface), not a PCIe part - it was previously cut here by accident, which is
# what surfaced the question.
# CONFIG_PACKAGE_ath9k-htc-firmware is not set
# CONFIG_PACKAGE_kmod-rt2800-usb is not set
# CONFIG_PACKAGE_kmod-rt2x00-usb is not set
# CONFIG_PACKAGE_kmod-rt2800-lib is not set
